📡 GitHub Actions — Complete Workflow Commands Reference Guide
 
Source: GitHub Docs — Workflow Commands | Last Updated: 2026-09-04 | Platform: GitHub Actions Runners (Ubuntu, Windows, macOS)
 
 
 
🎯 Overview
 
Workflow commands let your steps communicate with the runner machine to set environment variables, outputs, logs, annotations, summaries, and more. Most use  ::command::  syntax via  stdout ; others write to environment files ( GITHUB_*  paths).
 
 
 
📋 Quick Reference — All Commands
 
Category Command / File Purpose Bash Example PowerShell Example 
📝 Log Annotations  ::debug::  Debug message (visible with  ACTIONS_STEP_DEBUG=true )  echo "::debug::Message"   Write-Output "::debug::Message"  
  ::notice::  Notice annotation (w/ file/line)  echo "::notice file=app.js,line=1::Note"   Write-Output "::notice file=app.js,line=1::Note"  
  ::warning::  Warning annotation  echo "::warning file=app.js::Warning"   Write-Output "::warning file=app.js::Warning"  
  ::error::  Error annotation  echo "::error file=app.js::Error!"   Write-Output "::error file=app.js::Error!"  
📂 Log Grouping  ::group::  /  ::endgroup::  Collapsible log section  echo "::group::Title"  /  echo "::endgroup::"   Write-Output "::group::Title"  /  Write-Output "::endgroup::"  
🔒 Secrets  ::add-mask::  Mask value in logs →  ***   echo "::add-mask::$SECRET"   Write-Output "::add-mask::$SECRET"  
🌐 Env Vars  >> $GITHUB_ENV  Set env var for all subsequent steps  echo "NAME=val" >> $GITHUB_ENV   "NAME=val" >> $env:GITHUB_ENV  
📤 Outputs  >> $GITHUB_OUTPUT  Set step output for use by later steps/jobs  echo "NAME=val" >> $GITHUB_OUTPUT   "NAME=val" >> $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT  
📊 Job Summary  >> $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY  Markdown summary shown on workflow run page  echo "# Title" >> $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY   "# Title" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY  
🛤️ System Path  >> $GITHUB_PATH  Prepend directory to  $PATH   echo "$HOME/bin" >> $GITHUB_PATH   "$env:HOME/bin" >> $env:GITHUB_PATH  
🔄 State  >> $GITHUB_STATE  Pass values to  pre:  /  post:  actions  echo "KEY=val" >> $GITHUB_STATE   "KEY=val" >> $env:GITHUB_STATE  
🚫 Control  ::stop-commands::  /  ::token::  Temporarily disable all workflow commands  echo "::stop-commands::$TOKEN"   Write-Output "::stop-commands::$TOKEN"  
📦 Artifacts  >> $GITHUB_ARTIFACTS  Declare workflow artifacts (files/OCI)  echo "dist/app" >> $GITHUB_ARTIFACTS   "dist/app" >> $env:GITHUB_ARTIFACTS  
 
 
 
🔍 Detailed Usage — By Category
 
📝 Log Annotations — Debug, Notice, Warning, Error
 
Creates visual annotations in the GitHub UI, optionally linked to a file & line.
 
Syntax:
 
plaintext
  
::command file={name},line={N},col={N},title={Title}::{Message}
 
 
-  ::debug::  — Only visible when secret  ACTIONS_STEP_DEBUG=true 
bash
  
echo "::debug::Variable value is $MY_VAR"
 
-  ::notice::  — Info-level annotation
bash
  
echo "::notice file=src/app.js,line=42,title=Review Note::Consider refactoring this block"
 
-  ::warning::  — Yellow warning
bash
  
echo "::warning file=package.json,line=1::Deprecated dependency"
 
-  ::error::  — Red error annotation (does NOT fail the step — use  exit 1  for that)
bash
  
echo "::error file=app.js,line=10::Syntax error"
 
 
 
 
📂 Grouping Log Lines
 
Collapse/expand blocks of log output for cleaner readability.
 
yaml
  
- name: Build process
  run: |
    echo "::group::🔨 Building application"
    npm run build
    echo "::endgroup::"
 
 
 
 
🔒 Masking Secrets —  ::add-mask:: 
 
Prevents secrets from appearing in logs — replaced with  *** . Must run before outputting the value.
 
bash
  
echo "::add-mask::$API_KEY"  # Mask FIRST
echo "Using key: $API_KEY"   # Logs: Using key: ***
 
 
⚠️ Masked values cannot be used as outputs between jobs. Store in a secret store instead.
 
 
 
🌐 Environment Variables —  GITHUB_ENV 
 
Set variables available to all subsequent steps in the same job. Not available in the current step.
 
bash
  
echo "BUILD_VERSION=1.2.0" >> $GITHUB_ENV
echo "BUILD_TIMESTAMP=$(date -Iseconds)" >> $GITHUB_ENV
 
 
Multiline values — use delimiter:
 
bash
  
echo 'JSON_OUTPUT<<EOF' >> $GITHUB_ENV
curl -s https://api.example.com/status
echo 'EOF' >> $GITHUB_ENV
 
 
❌ Cannot set  NODE_OPTIONS  or overwrite reserved  GITHUB_*  /  RUNNER_*  vars.
 
 
 
📤 Step Outputs —  GITHUB_OUTPUT 
 
Share values between steps and jobs. Must define  id  on the step to reference.
 
yaml
  
- name: Generate version
  id: version
  run: echo "VERSION=v1.0.0-$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)" >> $GITHUB_OUTPUT

- name: Use output
  run: echo "Deploying ${{ steps.version.outputs.VERSION }}"
 
 
 
 
📊 Job Summary —  GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY 
 
Write Markdown displayed on the workflow run summary page. Great for test results, stats, release notes.
 
bash
  
echo "## 📊 Build Summary" >> $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
echo "" >> $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
echo "- **Version:** $VERSION" >> $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
echo "- **Status:** ✅ Success" >> $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
echo "- **Tests:** 247 passed, 0 failed" >> $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
 
 
- Append:  >>  — Add content
- Overwrite:  >  — Replace all content
- Delete:  rm $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY  — Remove summary
- Limit: 1 MiB per step; max 20 summaries per job
 
 
 
🛤️ Add to System PATH —  GITHUB_PATH 
 
Prepend directory to  $PATH  for all subsequent steps.
 
bash
  
echo "$HOME/.local/bin" >> $GITHUB_PATH
 
 
 
 
🔄 State —  GITHUB_STATE 
 
Share data between  main:  and  post:  actions within a custom action. Accessed as  STATE_*  env vars.
 
bash
  
echo "TEMP_FILES=/tmp/build" >> $GITHUB_STATE
 
 
 
 
🚫 Disable Commands Temporarily —  ::stop-commands:: 
 
Prevent accidental command parsing when outputting scripts or logs. Use a random unique token to resume.
 
bash
  
TOKEN=$(uuidgen)
echo "::stop-commands::$TOKEN"
# Nothing below is parsed as a command
echo "::warning::This is just text, not a command!"
# Resume
echo "::$TOKEN::"
 
 
 
 
📦 Workflow Artifacts —  GITHUB_ARTIFACTS 
 
Declare files or OCI images as artifacts for tracking.
 
bash
  
# File
echo "dist/myapp-linux-amd64.tar.gz" >> $GITHUB_ARTIFACTS

# OCI image with digest
echo "oci://ghcr.io/you/app:v1@sha256:abc123..." >> $GITHUB_ARTIFACTS
 
 
Read aggregated list from  $GITHUB_ARTIFACTS_LIST  (JSON).
 
 
 
⚙️ Bash vs. PowerShell — Key Differences
 
Feature Bash (Ubuntu/macOS) PowerShell (Windows/pwsh) 
Env var file  $GITHUB_ENV   $env:GITHUB_ENV  
Output file  $GITHUB_OUTPUT   $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT  
Summary file  $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY   $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY  
Path file  $GITHUB_PATH   $env:GITHUB_PATH  
Encoding UTF-8 default pwsh = UTF-8; 5.1 = specify  -Encoding utf8  
Append syntax  >> file   >> env:VAR  
 
 
 
🧠 Toolkit Equivalents (JavaScript Actions)
 
If you're writing a JavaScript Action, these workflow commands map directly to  @actions/core  methods:
 
JS Function Workflow Command 
 core.debug()   ::debug::  
 core.notice()   ::notice::  
 core.warning()   ::warning::  
 core.error()   ::error::  
 core.startGroup()  /  core.endGroup()   ::group::  /  ::endgroup::  
 core.setOutput()   GITHUB_OUTPUT  
 core.exportVariable()   GITHUB_ENV  
 core.addPath()   GITHUB_PATH  
 core.setSecret()   ::add-mask::  
 core.summary   GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY  
 
 
 
✅ Best Practices
 
- ✅ Mask secrets FIRST — before printing or using in commands
- ✅ Use step outputs for inter-job values; use secrets store for sensitive data
- ✅ Write job summaries for key info — saves users from digging into logs
- ✅ Set  ACTIONS_STEP_DEBUG=true  in repo Secrets to see  ::debug::  output
- ✅ Use  idempotent  commands — appending to env files is safe
- ❌ Don't put secrets in  GITHUB_OUTPUT  — they'll leak unless masked
- ❌ Don't overwrite  GITHUB_*  /  RUNNER_*  variables
 
 
 
